{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/15/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"0934a4d8\" lines=\"75-90\">\n<description>\nReveal the rectangular patch hidden by the solid marker using the grid's reflection symmetries.\n\nInput structure:\n- A square colored pattern with one solid rectangular marker color occluding a patch.\n- The visible pattern has horizontal and vertical reflection symmetry on a large lower/right strip.\n- The top and left outer strips also expose transpose counterparts for cells not recoverable by those reflections.\n\nRule:\n- Find the unique color whose full extent is a solid rectangle; this rectangle is the output region.\n- Infer the reflected strip start as the smallest row/column offset whose lower/right strips are mirror-consistent, ignoring marker pixels.\n- For each marker pixel, copy the unique non-marker value in its horizontal/vertical reflection orbit; if that orbit is entirely hidden in the outer strip, use the transposed top/left-strip counterpart.\n\nKey insight:\nThe marker is not part of the pattern; it covers a missing rectangle whose cells are still determined by the visible mirror or transpose copies elsewhere in the grid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"18447a8d\" lines=\"33-48\">\n<description>\nMove each right-side colored shape into the left slot whose template color is its exact complement.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has two equal-width slots separated by one background column.\n- Non-background rows form horizontal bands separated by all-background rows.\n- Each band has a shared template color in the left slot and one colored source shape in the right slot.\n\nRule:\n- For each band, define its destination shape as the cells in the left slot not occupied by the template color.\n- Normalize every right-side source shape to right-slot coordinates and match it to the unique equal destination shape.\n- Clear the original right-side source pixels and paint the matched left-slot complement with the source color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe right-side objects are not placed by row order; each one completes the unique left template whose missing cells have the same shape.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"880c1354\" lines=\"14-28\">\n<description>\nRecolor the separated outer regions by rotating their colors one step clockwise around the yellow-orange divider.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid contains a fixed yellow/orange divider structure.\n- All other colors form separated 4-connected monochrome regions around that divider.\n\nRule:\n- Leave the yellow and orange pixels unchanged.\n- Sort the non-divider regions by their centroid angle around the divider centroid in screen-coordinate clockwise order.\n- Each region keeps its cells and receives the color of the previous region in that cyclic order.\n\nKey insight:\n- The objects do not move; only the color labels cycle through the spatial order of the regions around the divider.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"97c75046\" lines=\"88-107\">\n<description>\nMove the single marker to the endpoint reached by sliding along the obstacle contour.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background color fills the canvas.\n- One single-pixel marker sits away from a connected obstacle region of the\n  remaining color.\n- The marker has exactly one horizontal or vertical sightline to the obstacle.\n\nRule:\n- Find the last background pixel before the obstacle along that sightline.\n- From that pixel, try the two diagonal turns that continue around the\n  obstacle boundary.\n- Move the marker to the endpoint of the turn that remains 4-adjacent to the\n  obstacle for the longest distance.\n\nKey insight:\nThe marker is not placed by distance to the obstacle; it first points to the\nobstacle, then follows the visible outside contour until that contour segment ends.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e4888269\" lines=\"67-88\">\n<description>\nRecolor every target pixel by following the ordered two-column substitution legend.\n\nInput structure\n- A dominant background surrounds one multicolor vertical legend: a connected,\n  fully filled two-column block with one color pair per row.\n- Other non-background pixels or objects are the targets; divider or frame\n  pixels are ordinary target-side structure that remain unchanged unless their\n  color is rewritten by the legend.\n\nRule\n- Read the legend rows from top to bottom as substitutions from the left\n  column color to the right column color.\n- For each non-background pixel outside the legend, scan those rows in order;\n  whenever the current color equals the row's left color, replace it with the\n  row's right color and keep scanning lower rows.\n- Leave the legend itself and background pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The same color may be rewritten multiple times, but only by substitutions\n  that appear later in the vertical legend, so the row order is part of the\n  symbol instruction.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5d588b4d\" lines=\"10-28\">\n<description>\nExpand the top-left horizontal bar into a wrapped sequence of increasing and decreasing foreground runs.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a background color and exactly one foreground color.\n- All foreground pixels form one contiguous horizontal bar in the top row.\n- The bar starts at the left edge; its length is the control value n.\n\nRule:\n- Build a one-dimensional sequence of foreground runs with lengths\n  1, 2, ..., n, n-1, ..., 2, 1.\n- Separate adjacent runs by one background pixel.\n- Wrap the sequence row-major across the input width and pad the final row\n  with background pixels.\n\nKey insight:\nThe output preserves the input width; the bar length controls the run-length\ndiamond, and the apparent 2D pattern is just that 1D sequence wrapped into rows.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"898e7135\" lines=\"7-20\">\n<description>\nInflate a frame's hole-layout and fill each hole with its matching piece.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Largest component is a monochrome frame enclosing bg holes.\n- Outside pieces composed of k×k blocks; k = side of smallest solid square piece.\n\nRule:\n- Extract connected hole regions inside the frame as slots.\n- Match each piece to a slot by comparing block-level shapes under rotation/flip.\n- Output the layout scaled by k, with pieces placed in slots; frame color as background.\n\nKey insight: Pieces are k×k-block-scaled versions of holes; downsampling reveals shape matches under all 8 orientations.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"981571dc\" lines=\"6-19\">\n<description>\nReconstruct a 4-way symmetric mosaic by filling missing (black) pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- A colored grid exhibiting bilateral symmetry along both a vertical and a horizontal axis.\n- Some pixels are erased to color 0 (black), creating gaps in the pattern.\n\nRule:\n- Infer the vertical and horizontal reflection axes from the visible (non-zero) pixels.\n- For each black pixel, recover its color from the mirrored position across either axis or both.\n- When multiple mirrors yield candidates, use the majority color.\n\nKey insight: The reflection axes are not given — they must be deduced from the surviving pixels by finding the axes that best preserve the existing symmetry.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"abbfd121\" lines=\"56-74\">\n<description>\nRecover the repeating background pattern hidden under the largest solid rectangle.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is covered by a small row/column periodic pattern.\n- Several non-pattern colors form solid rectangular foreground objects that\n  overwrite the pattern.\n- The requested output region is the largest of those solid rectangles.\n\nRule:\n- Find every 4-connected monochromatic object whose bounding box is a filled\n  rectangle with both dimensions greater than one.\n- Treat those rectangles as masks, infer the smallest repeating tile that is\n  consistent with all remaining visible pixels, and repaint the largest\n  rectangle's coordinates with that tile.\n\nKey insight: The rectangle colors are occluders; the visible pixels outside\nthem are enough to reconstruct the original periodic background underneath.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"da6e95e5\" lines=\"70-81\">\n<description>\nExtract the central object from the marker cluster whose markers have the same color.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background and several clusters; each cluster has four\nsame-color corner marker objects around one central monochromatic object.\nRule\nFind every central object enclosed by four aligned corner markers of one color,\nthen choose the unique one whose object color equals the marker color.\nKey insight\nThe answer is not the largest or most frequent object; it is the center of the\nself-colored cluster, cropped to that object's bounding box with background kept.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e048c9ed\" lines=\"11-26\">\n<description>\nAdd a quantity-color label in the top marker column for each horizontal bar.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a black background and one non-background marker pixel in the top row.\n- Below the marker row, every non-empty source row contains one solid monochrome horizontal bar to the left of the marker column.\n- Source rows are staggered every other row.\n\nRule\n- Copy the input grid.\n- For each source bar, read its quantity as the bar length.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
